The new tests cover touch flings in both directions, which is the ticket's core scenario. On desktop, the other bypass vector is a `PointerScrollEvent` (mouse wheel / horizontal trackpad scroll). The implementation already blocks it — `Scrollable._receivedPointerSignal` consults `shouldAcceptUserOffset`, which `NeverScrollableScrollPhysics` returns `false` — but nothing in the test suite pins that behavior. If someone later swaps the physics (e.g. to a custom "block-forward-only" physics), a desktop wheel-scroll regression would slip through silently.

